From c23046665b44bf73fcf74286fce2066fe6e3fbaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Merlin Kooshmanian <mkooshmanian@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:27:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/33] sched/tgbs: derive root server bandwidth per CPU

Derive each root server's budget from the global DEADLINE bandwidth
limit minus direct child reservations on that CPU, instead of applying
the smallest residual budget everywhere.

Expose the computed budgets through the read-only, flat-keyed
cpu.runtime_us interface while keeping the root period configurable.

Serialize recalculation with configuration and hierarchy changes.
Release reservations before admitting increases, and reject global
limits below existing child reservations on any CPU.

Preserve cpu.reclaim and SCHED_FLAG_RECLAIM across updates.
